<title>FRANCE: Legrand sees poor 1996, improved 1997.</title>
<headline>Legrand sees poor 1996, improved 1997.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Legrand chairman Francois Grapotte told French radio on Saturday that 1996 would not be a good year for the electrical equipment producer but that 1997 would be better.</p>
<p>&quot;Independently of the economic climate, we have certain objective elements for improvement that make us hope to recapture a favourable trajectory in our 1997 results,&quot; he told Radio Classique.</p>
<p>Legrand reported a 3.2 percent drop in first-half 1996 profit to 453 million francs and cautioned at the time that it did not expect significant improvement in 1996 results.</p>
</text>
